%I A399380 #16 Sep 21 2026 20:55:42
%S A399380 0,1,6,25,26,122,180,185,206,420,635,1052,1261,1382,1488,1682,1708,
%T A399380 1800,2006,2285,2306,2315,2331,4620,4681,6002,9450,10521,11568,12816,
%U A399380 16171,16355,18482,20586,20976,21446,23196,25549,27842,30026,31412,46385,46406,60264,76236,90090,100014,121172,121381,152465,152486
%N A399380 Numbers k such that all radix primes corresponding to the nonzero digits in the primorial base expansion of k are also prime factors of the arithmetic derivative of k.
%H A399380 Antti Karttunen, <a href="/A399380/b399380.txt">Table of n, a(n) for n = 1..500</a>
%H A399380 <a href="/index/Pri#primorialbase">Index entries for sequences related to primorial base</a>.
%F A399380 {k such that A003415(k) == 0 mod A328571(k)}.
%e A399380 635 is a included as term, because A049345(635) = 30021 [as 635 = 3*A002110(4) + 2*A002110(1) + 1*A002110(0)], and therefore the radix primes of nonzero digits are 2, 3 and 11, all of which divide the arithmetic derivative of 635, which is A003415(635) = 132 = 2^2 * 3 * 11.
%e A399380 1800 is a included as term, because A049345(1800) = 84000 [as 1800 = 8*A002110(4) + 4*A002110(3)], and therefore the radix primes of nonzero digits are 7 and 11, both of which divide the arithmetic derivative of 1800, which is A003415(1800) = 4620 = 2^2 * 3 * 5 * 7 * 11.
%e A399380 2315 is a included as term, because A049345(2315) = 100021 [as 2315 = 1*A002110(5) + 2*A002110(1) + 1*A002110(0)], and therefore the radix primes of nonzero digits are 2, 3 and 13, all of which divide the arithmetic derivative of 2315, which is A003415(2315) = 468 = 2^2 * 3^2 * 13. Note that 2315 is one of the rare terms satisfying also the stricter condition of A369970.
%o A399380 (PARI) is_A399380(n) = if(n<=1, 1, my(f=factor(n), ad = n*sum(i=1, #f~, f[i, 2]/f[i, 1]), p=2); while(n, if(ad%p && n%p, return(0)); n \= p; p = nextprime(1+p)); (1));
%Y A399380 Cf. A003415, A049345, A328571.
%Y A399380 Subsequences: A369970, A369973.
%Y A399380 Cf. also A399379 for a dual condition, also A380527.
%K A399380 nonn,new
%O A399380 1,3
%A A399380 _Antti Karttunen_, Sep 20 2026
